                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game has nice ideas and unfortunately also has a lot of wasted potential.  if it wasn't free (but it is free), I would not recommend you buy it.  Currently, at the time of this review, it's free, but it's kind of a waste of time to make anything in it except maybe to toy around with it.  The draw of this, erm, drawing app is that you can draw objects and then turn them into physical objects with physics (gravity and collision) and interactivity (ability to be grabbed by the Vive controllers).  I saw similar functionality in the dorm room level of Rec Room, but this does it slightly better in my opinion.\n\nThere are some clear problems which the developer should address and fix:\n1. No uploading, no exporting, just save 1 scene, no \"new canvas\" or \"wipe all objects\" option.\n2. Very little to choose from on the right controller.  No box tool for the eraser!\n3. Objects can't have any kind of advanced interactivity, like gun lasers or enemy scripting.  That would make this more like a sandbox environment, and if that was the case, it might be a little more fun to draw some swords and things like that.\n\nMy biggest problem with the game is its lack of export and import options.  I would like to use this as a tool for modeling voxel objects.  It's perfect for that if I was given the export options alone!",
